model {
  extend basalt.pool {
    metadata {
      constraint "Self-service history imports require current pool management and use access and a page-bound dry-run approval before each write. The browser strips message content, previews every page, and only applies unchanged reviewed metadata after the person starts the import. Source names are distinct per database and reused for later backups; the server derives their pool-scoped UUIDs. Agent apply calls require human approval. Imported rows remain unattributed and unpriced; pausing or retrying never duplicates retained identities. Settings opens the same authenticated pool import flow and explains missing use access without widening host permissions. SQLite backups stay in a read-only ranged File worker with bounded keyset pages; WAL-dependent files are refused. The compiler resolves explicit browser exports without Node-only conditions, retains worker entries and serves byte-preserved WASM assets through the authenticated version asset path."
    }
  }
}
